@page "/docs/components/dock-layout"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/components/dock-layout" Title="Blazorise DockLayout component" Description="Learn to use the Blazorise DockLayout component to build docked workspaces with panes, tabs, splitters, auto-hide, and persisted layout state." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Components/DockLayout" AddedVersion="2.3" AddedDate="2026-07-26">
    Blazorise DockLayout component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Build IDE-like workspaces with docked panes, document areas, tab groups, splitters, auto-hide panes, and restorable layout state.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use the <Code>DockLayout</Code> component for editors, monitoring tools, and other workspaces where users need to rearrange related panes around their main content.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A pane can start on the left, right, top, bottom, or center document area.
    Users can move panes by dragging their headers, resize panes with splitters, group panes as tabs, auto-hide side panes, and close panes when enabled.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Structure
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Place <Code>DockPane</Code> components directly inside <Code>DockLayout</Code> for a simple workspace, or use <Code>DockSplit</Code> and <Code>DockTabs</Code> to define the initial arrangement.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsAnatomy Label="DockLayout component anatomy">
    <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="DockLayout" Description="Owns the workspace layout and state.">
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="DockPane" Description="A tool or document pane placed directly in the workspace." />
        <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="DockSplit" Description="An optional split between two layout nodes.">
            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="DockTabs" Description="An optional group of tabbed panes.">
                <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="DockPane" Description="One pane in the tab group." />
            </DocsAnatomyRegion>
            <DocsAnatomyRegion Label="DockPane" Description="A pane on the other side of the split." />
        </DocsAnatomyRegion>
    </DocsAnatomyRegion>
</DocsAnatomy>

